    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0245" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1723 <hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >12/14</hi></note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State
                            (White)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-21">April 21, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Doctor Soler and Doctor Vasconsellos called, at my request, and I told
                    them that the Ambassadors of Argentina, Brazil, Chile and Peru had requested me
                    to tell them that their Governments gladly adhere to the friendly manifestation
                    which I had made on behalf of the neutrals to the delegates of Paraguay and
                    Bolivia on the eleventh instant.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d139-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The two delegates expressed their pleasure at this and asked me to thank the
                    Ambassadors in question. They said that they would advise their Government at
                    once thereof.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d139-f1" n="5" xml:id="d139-f1-content">
                <p>A similar statement was made to the Bolivian delegates on the same date.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
